overing analysts target $42.64 on average, 10% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 9% falls short of the cost of capital of 9.1%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.77).","It converts 2% of revenue into free cash flow.","Operating margin is running 15pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 1.2% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 0.0x net debt to EBITDA ($570.8M of cash against $3.0B of debt), and interest cover is thin at 2.1x."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 8.3% over 3 years, 35.3% over 5 years and 0.9% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 41%).","Free cash flow has compounded -10.8% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.11 (orders outpacing sales) and a backlog worth 18% of annual revenue.","Capex runs only 0.5x depreciation (4.5% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown."],"own":["Insiders own 11.1%, meaningful skin in the game, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Shareholder yield is a modest 0.9% (0.9% in dividends).","The share count has grown 0.7% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","Short interest is elevated at 11.1% of the float, 3.8 days to cover."],"people":["With about 8,451 employees, each generates about $369K of revenue, 0.6x the Communication Services median, and productivity has risen 2.3% a year.","That works out to $8K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $4.3M (12x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $4K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INSUFFICIENT DATA","conv":null,"head":"Not enough data to value it: missing price or fair value.","pros":[],"cons":[],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":null,"vc":null,"med":{"pe":14.9123,"ev_ebitda":9.366,"pfcf":11.3182,"pb":1.9143